# Env & secrets — NEVER commit
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem
# Deliberate, narrow exception: a throwaway RSA key generated locally with `openssl
# genpkey` solely to unit-test JWT assertion construction in providers/vertex.rs. Not
# connected to any real Google Cloud project or credential — see
# apps/gateway/testdata/README.md. Committing it is the point: CI can sign a test
# assertion with no real secret involved. Every other *.pem stays blocked.
!apps/gateway/testdata/vertex_test_key.pem
# Same exception, for two throwaway keypairs used to prove RS256 signature verification
# in the SSO id-token tests (real crypto, no real account behind either key). Generated
# locally with `openssl genrsa` / `openssl rsa -pubout`; replaced the `rsa` crate as a
# dev-dependency so cargo-audit's RUSTSEC-2023-0071 finding (no fix available for that
# crate) does not have to be carried or suppressed just to generate test keys at runtime.
!apps/gateway/testdata/sso_test_key_*.pem
secrets/

